„­bible_version£KJV¤book/§chapter¨sections–…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢O foolish Galatians, who hath bewitched you, that ye should not obey the truth, before whose eyes Jesus Christ hath been evidently set forth, crucified among you?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkThis only would I learn of you, Received ye the Spirit by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAre ye so foolish? having begun in the Spirit, are ye now made perfect by the flesh?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>Have ye suffered so many things in vain? if it be yet in vain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘He therefore that ministereth to you the Spirit, and worketh miracles among you, doeth he it by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLEven as Abraham believed God, and it was accounted to him for righteousness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUKnow ye therefore that they which are of faith, the same are the children of Abraham.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦And the scripture, foreseeing that God would justify the heathen through faith, preached before the gospel unto Abraham, saying, In thee shall all nations be blessed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙASo then they which be of faith are blessed with faithful Abraham.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book/§chapter«first_verse
