„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnBut that no man is justified by the law in the sight of God, it is evident: for, The just shall live by faith.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd the law is not of faith: but, The man that doeth them shall live in them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒChrist hath redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒthat the blessing of Abraham might come on the Gentiles through Jesus Christ; that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBrethren, I speak after the manner of men; Though it be but a man's covenant, yet if it be confirmed, no man disannulleth, or addeth thereto.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒNow to Abraham and his seed were the promises made. He saith not, And to seeds, as of many; but as of one, And to thy seed, which is Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÇAnd this I say, that the covenant, that was confirmed before of God in Christ, the law, which was four hundred and thirty years after, cannot disannul, that it should make the promise of none effect.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfFor if the inheritance be of the law, it is no more of promise: but God gave it to Abraham by promise.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸Wherefore then serveth the law? It was added because of transgressions, till the seed should come to whom the promise was made; and it was ordained by angels in the hand of a mediator.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8Now a mediator is not a mediator of one, but God is one.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Is the law then against the promises of God? God forbid: for if there had been a law given which could have given life, verily righteousness should have been by the law.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~But the scripture hath concluded all under sin, that the promise by faith of Jesus Christ might be given to them that believe.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnBut before faith came, we were kept under the law, shut up unto the faith which should afterwards be revealed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdWherefore the law was our schoolmaster to bring us unto Christ, that we might be justified by faith.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDBut after that faith is come, we are no longer under a schoolmaster.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<For ye are all the children of God by faith in Christ Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHFor as many of you as have been baptized into Christ have put on Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither bond nor free, there is neither male nor female: for ye are all one in Christ Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd if ye be Christ's, then are ye Abraham's seed, and heirs according to the promise.¦layout ªlast_verse